 "source": {
  "ids_and_names": "BDS 1.26.51 AvailableCommands capture (crates/unastar-data/output/available_commands.json, command enum `Enchant`): the enchantment id is the value's index. Not repeated here; crates/unastar-rules/build.rs reads the capture.",
  "cross_checks": "crates/unastar-rules/build.rs fails the build unless the capture agrees with Mojang's bedrock-protocol-docs `Enchant__Type.json` (1.26.40 beta: same order and count) and the vanilla pack's `metadata/vanilladata_modules/mojang-enchantments.json` (the same `minecraft:` names, plus its aliases), every key below is a captured name and every `lang_key` is in the vanilla `en_US.lang`.",
  "rules": "Random-enchanting rules of BDS 1.26.51 loot and mob gear, moved unchanged from the table in crates/unastar-rules/src/enchanting.rs (commit 9d64c3af; its README row 'Random enchanting' records them as confirmed against the reference): selection weight (BDS frequency 30/10/3/1 weighs 10/5/2/1), primary and secondary enchantment slot bits, minimum cost of level l = min_cost[0] + min_cost[1] * (l - 1), max_level, treasure (never offered without treasure allowed), discoverable (false: never offered by random enchanting), exclusive_group (non-zero groups exclude each other), excludes (one more excluded enchantment) and list (an item keeps three enchantment lists; compatibility is checked only within one).",
  "lang_key": "Resource-pack name keys `/enchant` sends (`%<key>`), moved from crates/unastar/src/command/exec/enchant.rs; transcribed from the BDS 1.26.51 command capture.",
